# Workflow: Migration

Purpose:
  Execute project migrations after .sdd/ schema updates.
  Ensures project instances stay consistent with the current
  .sdd/ structure and conventions.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @../commands/sdd-migrate.sdd
   3 @../projects/example_project/migrations/INDEX.sdd

Steps:
  1. List pending migrations from migrations/INDEX.sdd
  2. Validate each pending migration (idempotency, dependencies)
  3. Apply migrations in order (001, 002, 003, ...)
  4. Update migration state (PENDING -> APPLIED)
  5. Validate project instance after migration
  6. Validate shared registries (projects/prompts/)
  7. Validate features/ directory structure
  8. Report results

Rules:
  [MW1] Migrations MUST be applied in numerical order.
  [MW2] If a migration fails, the pipeline MUST halt.
  [MW3] Migrations MUST be idempotent — safe to re-run.
  [MW4] Failed migrations MUST be manually resolved before re-running.
  [MW5] Migration state MUST be persisted in migrations/INDEX.sdd.
  [MW6] Shared registries (projects/prompts/) MUST be validated after project migrations.
  [MW7] Shared registries are NOT project instances and MUST NOT be migrated as such.
  [MW8] features/ directory MUST exist and contain INDEX.sdd, layers.sdd, decisions.sdd.

State: +
